      "id": 10,
      "options": {
        "content": "### 🔬 Person 4: Drift Explainability Portal\n\nWhenever concept drift is detected, our explainability pipeline extracts **semantic themes**, **distinctive keyword shifts**, and **representative centroid tweets** to answer *why* the detectors alarmed.\n\n---\n\n#### 📊 Detector Consensus Summary\n- **154 Windows Total** (14 Reference, 140 Stream Windows)\n- **Both Detectors Alarmed (`both`)**: **10 windows** — *High-confidence semantic regime changes (June 2021 surge)*\n- **DriftLens Only (`driftlens_only`)**: **110 windows** — *High sensitivity to fine embedding subspace shifts*\n- **MCD-DD Only (`mcddd_only`)**: **2 windows** — *Covariance outlier shifts detected in early May 2020*\n- **Neither Alarmed (`neither`)**: **18 windows** — *Quiescent baseline behavior*\n\n---\n\n#### 🚀 Interactive Explainability UI\nLaunch the companion standalone web viewer to interactively inspect before/after cards and keyword clouds:\n\n```bash\n# From repository root:\npython3 -m http.server 5050\n# Open: http://localhost:5050/monitoring/explainability_viewer.html\n```\n\n**Generated Explainability Artifacts:**\n- `output/drift/explainability_report.json` — Structured JSON report with top emerging/fading terms & centroid tweets.\n- `output/drift/disagreement_table.csv` — Full tabular record of detector alarms and ratio discrepancies.\n",
